// The Windows executable's icons: the application's own, and the one Explorer
// draws on a .cutreel project file.
//
// Configured rather than committed as-is so the paths can be absolute: rc.exe
// resolves a relative one against its own working directory, which is the
// build tree, and the icons are not there.
//
// Id order is the contract. Explorer shows the first icon in id order for the
// executable itself, so the application mark has to be the lowest id -- that
// is what a shortcut, the taskbar and Add/Remove Programs all display. The
// document icon follows it, and the MSI names it by *index* rather than by id:
// "zaro-preview.exe,1" is the second icon group in id order, which is id 2
// below. See cmake/wix-patch.xml. Inserting an icon between these two would
// silently repoint that association, so append rather than insert.
1 ICON "@ZARO_ICON_ICO@"
2 ICON "@ZARO_DOCUMENT_ICO@"
